Proposed minimal patch to fix the heap-use-after-free during XInclude processing in libxml2 inside /src/libxml2. The root cause is that namespaces (xmlNs) freed during XInclude include can still be accessed by the document dumper (xmlNodeDumpOutputInternal). The fix below detaches namespace pointers from the nodes in the included subtree before freeing it, so the dumper no longer dereferences freed memory. This avoids the use-after-free without changing the dumper's behavior for non-XInclude trees. The change is intentionally small and localized to xinclude.c and a small defensive guard in xmlsave.c for safety.

1) Add a helper to detach namespaces from a subtree
File: src/libxml2/xinclude.c
--------------------------------
+/* Detach namespaces from a node tree to avoid UAF when the tree is freed
+ * during XInclude processing. By clearing ns pointers on included subtree
+ * nodes and attributes, the subsequent dumper will not dereference freed
+ * namespace structures.
+ */
+static void xmlClearNsInTree(xmlNodePtr node) {
+    if (node == NULL) return;
+    if (node->ns != NULL) {
+        node->ns = NULL;
+    }
+    /* Clear namespaces on attributes as well */
+    for (xmlAttrPtr attr = node->properties; attr != NULL; attr = attr->next) {
+        if (attr->ns != NULL) {
+            attr->ns = NULL;
+        }
+    }
+    /* Recurse into children */
+    if (node->children != NULL) {
+        xmlNodePtr child = node->children;
+        while (child != NULL) {
+            xmlClearNsInTree(child);
+            child = child->next;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
*** End Patch ***

2) Detach namespaces before freeing the included subtree
